</ref>|VRMO<ref name="GCM"/>}} is a [[domestic airport]]. It is located on the island of [[Kooddoo]] in [[Gaafu Alifu Atoll]] in the [[Maldives]]. It was opened on 10 September 2012 by President [[Mohamed Waheed Hassan]].<ref name=":0">{{cite news | url = http://www.haveeru.com.mv/kooddoo_airport/44467 | title = Kooddoo airport constructed in just seven months opened | work = [[Haveeru Daily]] | date = 10 September 2012 | url-status = dead | archiveurl = https://web.archive.org/web/20140407101516/http://www.haveeru.com.mv/kooddoo_airport/44467 | archivedate = 7 April 2014 }}</ref><ref>{{cite news |date=10 September 2012 |title=Festive ceremony marks opening of Kooddoo Airport |url=https://english.sun.mv/5626 |access-date=25 October 2024 |work=Sun}}</ref><ref>{{cite news |last=Lubbock |first=Hazel |date=10 September 2012 |title=A step closer to paradise |url=http://www.cntraveller.com/news/2012/september/kooddoo-airport-gaafu-alifu-atoll-maldives |url-status=dead |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20121001003820/https://www.cntraveller.com/news/2012/september/kooddoo-airport-gaafu-alifu-atoll-maldives |archive-date=1 October 2012 |work=[[Condé Nast Traveller]]}}</ref>

== History ==
The Airport was constructed by Bonavista (Maldives) Pvt Ltd in 2012 and was opened by president [[Mohamed Waheed Hassan]].<ref name=":0" /><ref>{{Cite web |date=10 September 2012 |title=President Waheed opens The Residence Maldives |url=https://presidencymaldives.gov.mv/Press/Article/7896 |access-date=25 October 2024 |website=[[The President's Office]]}}</ref> It was later renovated in 2017 by Pristine Island Investment and was opened by president [[Abdulla Yameen]], which included a new VIP lounge and two staff accommodation blocks.<ref>{{Cite news |date=25 September 2017 |title=President opens expanded Kooddoo airport and new resort |url=https://maldivesindependent.com/business/president-opens-expanded-kooddoo-airport-and-new-resort-132755 |access-date=25 October 2024 |work=Maldives Independent}}</ref> 

In 2024, the [[Maldivian (airline)|Maldivian]] airline halted flights to the airport after the airport's runway damaged two of the wings of a plane.<ref>{{Cite news |last=Osmanagic |first=Ameera |date=11 October 2024 |title=Maldivian to discontinue Kooddoo operations |url=https://edition.mv/maldivian_airline/36644 |access-date=25 October 2024 |work=[[The Edition]]}}</ref> The Minister of Transport and Civil Aviation [[Mohamed Ameen (21st-century politician)|Mohamed Ameen]], has said that the operator, Pristine Island Maldives, will renovate the runway as well as the apron.<ref>{{Cite news |last=Mohamed |first=Mariyath |date=13 October 2024 |title=Kooddoo airport being renovated, flights will commence soon: Minister Ameen |url=https://edition.mv/justice/36676 |access-date=25 October 2024 |work=[[The Edition]]}}</ref><ref>{{Cite news |last=Osmanagic |first=Ameera |date=14 October 2024 |title=Operator will renovate Kooddoo Airport: Minister Ameen |url=https://edition.mv/mohamed_ameen_transport_minister/36733 |access-date=25 October 2024 |work=[[The Edition]]}}</ref>

